# 0001-nuxel-phone-features — port hint (read by build-kernel.sh WARN path)

Status: STUB — not yet ported to linux-postmarketos-exynos9820.

The original patch (in kernel/google-pixel-10-pro-xl/patches/) adds
drivers/nuxel/ with CONFIG_NUXEL / CONFIG_NUXEL_PHONE / CONFIG_NUXEL_BOOT_PARAM
and parses nuxel.boot=1 / nuxel.device= on the kernel command line.

Why it is a stub here:
- The two wiring hunks (drivers/Kconfig, drivers/Makefile) are context-dependent
  and must be verified against the cloned exynos9820 tree.
- The patch text hardcodes nuxel.device=mustang in help/description strings;
  the port must accept s10plus as well.
- The C driver itself is NOT 6.12-only (struct proc_ops since v5.6,
  saved_command_line long-standing), so a clean port is likely but unproven.

Check before porting (after `bash kernel/s10plus/build-kernel.sh --clone`):

    git -C kernel/s10plus/.build/src apply --check \
        kernel/s10plus/patches/0001-nuxel-phone-features.patch

If it fails, re-base the two wiring hunks by hand, generalize mustang
references to s10plus, then uncomment CONFIG_NUXEL* in
kernel/s10plus/defconfig. Until then the stub stands and the defconfig keeps
the Nuxel symbols commented with TODO.
